# Generated data. Prettier must not touch any of it: binary-cache is written as
# single-line JSON and data/ snapshots are written by JSON.stringify, so
# formatting them would be undone by the next regeneration — permanent churn,
# and it would break the "two passes produce zero diff" reproducibility check
# the data PRs rely on. The yaml/toml were already excluded; the JSON was not,
# which left 839 generated files failing `prettier --check` and made the check
# useless as a gate.
data/**/*.json
data/**/*.yaml
data/**/*.toml
binary-cache/
package-lock.json
